<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Toski</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-war">Mahdist War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Toski was fought on 3 August 1889 near Toshki on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. An Anglo-Egyptian army under Francis Grenfell defeated a Mahdist invasion force led by Abd al-Rahman al-Nujumi, who was killed in the fighting. The battle ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-state">Mahdist State</a>'s attempt to carry its holy war into Egypt.</p></div>
